# WP-Q08 — published-surface allowlist control for the npx server tarball.
#
# `15-engineering-standards.md §2.10` + WP-Q08 Detailed Requirements #1: the published package keeps
# only the RUNNABLE artifact (`dist/` incl. the `bin`) + the README; it excludes sources, tests,
# fixtures, and build config. `pack:server` ALSO uses a publish-manifest `files` allowlist, but this
# `.npmignore` is the belt-and-suspenders guard so a direct `npm pack` of this package is also clean.
#
# NOTE: npm IGNORES `.npmignore` when a `package.json` `files` allowlist is present (the allowlist
# wins). The server manifest sets `"files": ["dist"]`, so this file is documentary + a safety net if
# the allowlist is ever removed. Patterns below mirror the allowlist's exclusions.

# --- sources & build inputs (not shipped; dist/ is the artifact) ---
src/
*.ts
!dist/**/*.d.ts
tsconfig*.json
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- tests & fixtures (never shipped) ---
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.d.ts
**/*.test.d.ts.map
__tests__/
test/
tests/
fixtures/
**/*.spec.*

# --- tooling / CI / editor cruft ---
.turbo/
.eslintrc*
eslint.config.*
.prettierrc*
vitest.config.*
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store

# --- dev-only manifests already excluded by the allowlist ---
.npmignore
